{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#116","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#116","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#116\",\"parent_revision\":\"b339819aa34a94d18420c0039839a50d9a3bb595eb53bd593ce9440eee84577a\",\"root_revision\":\"b339819aa34a94d18420c0039839a50d9a3bb595eb53bd593ce9440eee84577a\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAffects every agent following the fetch-to-disk policy, not one task.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`.gitignore` excludes `vendor/`, so `.claude/vendor/sources/` never populates a new worktree. The cached page and its `.meta.json` sidecar exist only in the primary checkout.\\n\\nAGENTS.md directs agents to fetch vendor documentation to disk and then read from disk, rather than pulling pages into context through WebFetch or an MCP URL tool. Inside a worktree that path dead-ends: the file the agent is told to read does not exist there.\\n\\nThis surfaced on a task whose acceptance depended on sourcing each added constant from a cached page. Under \\\"No invented constraints\\\" a key without a documented source cannot be added, so the task was unstartable in a worktree.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Options\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- Have `skilllint docs` resolve the cache against the primary checkout when running inside a worktree, so one fetch serves every worktree.\\n- Un-ignore `.claude/vendor/sources/` so cached pages travel with the branch, accepting the repo-size cost.\\n- Direct agents at the absolute primary-checkout path, which works today and is the current workaround.\\n\\nThe first keeps the documented workflow honest everywhere without committing fetched pages.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"080636e261c73b50b4772a3bce8b72972f810f2507cf926b5b0212ba28d8e7b7\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDORXxKvc8AAAABXP-Y0Q\"}"}